hadiths[185]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1439","Affan told us: Abd al-Warith told us: Ibn Abi Najih told us, he said: I asked Tawus about a man who stoned the pillar with six pebbles, then he said to me: Let him feed a handful of food. He said: Then I met Mujahid and asked him, and mentioned to him the statement of Tawus, then he said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Abd al-Rahman, has there not reached him the statement of Sad ibn Malik: We stoned the pillars, or the pillar, in our pilgrimage with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then we sat remembering, and among us was one who said: I stoned with six, and among us was one who said: I stoned with seven, and among us was one who said: I stoned with eight, and among us was one who said: I stoned with nine, and they saw no harm in that."
"1440","Affan told us: Wuhayb told us: Ayyub told us, from Amr ibn Said, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, from three of the sons of Sad, from Sad, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him visiting him while he was ill, while he was in Makkah. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have feared to die in the land from which I emigrated, as Sad ibn Khawlah died, so supplicate Allah to heal me. He said: O Allah, heal Sad; O Allah, heal Sad; O Allah, heal Sad. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and I have no heir except a daughter; shall I bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath two thirds of it. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath half of it. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath a third of it. He said: A third, and a third is much. Your spending from your wealth is charity for you, and your spending on your dependents is charity for you, and your spending on your family is charity for you, and that you leave your family living, or he said: in good, is better than that you leave them begging from people."
"1441","Abu Bakr al-Hanafi Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid told us: Bukayr ibn Mismar told us, from Amir ibn Sad, that his brother Umar went to Sad among sheep of his outside Madinah. When Sad saw him he said: I seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this rider. When he came to him he said: O father, are you content to be a Bedouin among your sheep while people dispute over kingship in Madinah. Then Sad struck the chest of Umar and said: Be silent, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, loves the God-fearing, rich, hidden servant."
"1442","Abu Amir told us: Fulayh told us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mamar, he said: Amir ibn Sad narrated to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz while he was governor over Madinah, that Sad said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever eats seven Ajwah dates from between the two lava tracts of Madinah on an empty stomach, nothing will harm him that day until evening. Fulayh said: And I think he said: And if he eats them in the evening, nothing will harm him until morning. Then Umar said: Look, O Amir, what you narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then he said: I bear witness I did not lie against Sad, and Sad did not lie against the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1443","Abu Amir told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar told us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from Amir ibn Sad, that Sad rode to his palace at al-Aqiq and found a slave beating trees or cutting them, so he stripped him. When Sad returned, the people of the slave came to him and spoke to him to return what he had taken from their slave. Then he said: Allah forbid that I return anything the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted me as spoils, and refused to return to them."
"1444","Rawh dictated it to us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd told us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of the happiness of the son of Adam is his seeking the choice of Allah, and of the happiness of the son of Adam is his contentment with what Allah has decreed, and of the wretchedness of the son of Adam is his abandoning seeking the choice of Allah, and of the wretchedness of the son of Adam is his anger at what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has decreed."
"1445","Rawh told us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd told us: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas told us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Of the happiness of the son of Adam are three, and of the wretchedness of the son of Adam are three: Of the happiness of the son of Adam are the righteous wife, the righteous dwelling, and the righteous mount; and of the wretchedness of the son of Adam are the evil wife, the evil dwelling, and the evil mount."
"1446","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: Abdullah ibn Lahiah told us: Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj told us, that he heard Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrate, that he heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be a trial; the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it will be better than the one hastening. He said: And I think he said: And the one reclining in it is better than the one sitting."
"1447","Abu Said told us: Shubah told us, from Simak ibn Harb, from a nephew of Sad, from Sad, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said of Banu Najiyah: I am of them and they are of me."
"1448","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us, and he mentioned the hadith with a story in it, then the nephew of Sad ibn Malik said: Banu Najiyah were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he said: They are a clan of me, and Sad was not mentioned in it."
"1449","Hasan told us: Ibn Lahiah told us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib told us, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If what a fingernail carries of what is in Paradise appeared, all that is between the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned for it, and if a man from the people of Paradise looked out and his bracelet appeared, its light would efface the light of the sun as the sun effaces the light of the stars."
"1450","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from Sad, he said: Make a grave with a side niche for me and set unbaked bricks over me upright as was done with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1451","Ibn Mahdi told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar told us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Sad, then he mentioned the like of it, and Abu Said agreed with al-Khuzai upon Amir ibn Sad as he said."
"1452","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us: Ismail, meaning Ibn Jafar, told us: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Abu al-Nadr, freedman of Umar ibn Ubaydullah ibn Mamar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said about wiping over the two leather socks: There is no harm in that."
"1453","Ishaq ibn Isa told us: Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to me, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard my father say: I never heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say of any living people walking that he is in Paradise, except of Abdullah ibn Salam."
"1454","Hushaym informed us: Khalid informed us, from Abu Uthman, he said: When Ziyad was claimed, I met Abu Bakrah. He said: So I said: What is this you have done; I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: My ear heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he says: Whoever claims a father in Islam other than his father, while he knows that he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him. Then Abu Bakrah said: And I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1455","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us, from Wuhayb, from Abu Waqid al-Laythi, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The hand is cut for the price of a shield."
"1456","Rawh told us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd al-Madani told us: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas told us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered me to call out in the days of Mina: They are days of eating and drinking, so there is no fasting in them, meaning the days of Tashriq."
"1457","Husayn ibn Muhammad told us: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman told us: Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya told us, from Abu Ishaq ibn Salim, from Amir ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: What is between the two lava tracts of Madinah is sacred; the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made it sacred as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. O Allah, place blessing in it twofold, and bless them in their sa and their mudd."
"1458","Affan told us: Hammad ibn Salamah told us: Asim ibn Bahdalah informed us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a bowl and ate from it, and a remainder remained. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man from this mountain pass will come, from the people of Paradise, eating this remainder. Sad said: And I had left my brother Umayr performing ablution. He said: So I said: It is Umayr. He said: Then Abdullah ibn Salam came and ate it."
"1459","Affan told us: Wuhayb told us: Musa ibn Uqbah told us, he said: I heard Abu al-Nadr narrate, from Abu Salamah, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, a hadith he raised to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about ablution over the two leather socks, that there is no harm in it."
"1460","Affan told us: Jarir ibn Hazim told us: Yala ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Abi Abdullah, he said: I saw Sad ibn Abi Waqqas seize a man hunting in the sanctuary of Madinah which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made sacred, and strip him of his clothes. Then his masters came and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made this sanctuary sacred and said: Whoever you see hunting anything in it, his spoils are his. So I will not return to you a morsel with which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fed me, but if you wish I will give you its price. And Affan once said: If you wish that I give you its price, I will give you."
"1461","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn narrated to me, that he narrated from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that he used to pray the last evening prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then pray Witr with one, adding nothing to it. He said: So it would be said to him: Do you pray Witr with one, adding nothing to it, O Abu Ishaq. Then he would say: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: He who does not sleep until he prays Witr is resolute."
"1462","Ismail ibn Umar told us: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq al-Hamdani told us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sad told us: My father Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Sad, he said: I passed by Uthman ibn Affan in the mosque and greeted him, and he filled his eyes with me, then did not return the greeting to me. So I came to the Commander of the Believers Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Believers, has anything happened in Islam, twice. He said: No, and what is that. He said: I said: Nothing except that I passed by Uthman just now in the mosque and greeted him, and he filled his eyes with me, then did not return the greeting to me. He said: So Umar sent to Uthman and called him, and said: What prevented you from returning the greeting to your brother. Uthman said: I did not do it. Sad said: I said: Yes. He said: Until he swore and I swore. He said: Then Uthman remembered and said: Yes, and I seek the forgiveness of Allah and repent to Him; you passed by me just now while I was speaking to myself about a statement I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; no, by Allah, I never mentioned it but my sight and my heart were covered with a covering. He said: Sad said: Then I will inform you of it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned to us the first supplication, then a Bedouin came and distracted him until the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, and I followed him. When I feared he would outpace me to his house, I struck the ground with my foot, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to me and said: Who is this, Abu Ishaq. He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What is it. He said: I said: Nothing, by Allah, except that you mentioned to us the first supplication, then this Bedouin came and distracted you. He said: Yes, the supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he was in the belly of the whale: There is no god but You, glory be to You, I have been of the wrongdoers. No Muslim ever supplicates his Lord with it for anything but He answers him."
"1463","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: Sulayman ibn Bilal told us: al-Juayd ibn Abd al-Rahman told us, from Aishah bint Sad, from her father, that Ali went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until he came to Thaniyyat al-Wada, with Ali weeping, saying: You leave me behind with those left behind. Then he said: Are you not content to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except prophethood."
"1464","Isam ibn Khalid told us: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to me, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he used to say: My nation is not incapable before its Lord of His delaying it half a day. And I asked Rashid: Has it reached you what half a day is. He said: Five hundred years."
"1465","Abu al-Yaman told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah told us, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: I indeed hope that my nation will not be incapable before its Lord of His delaying them half a day. Then it was said to Sad: And how much is half a day. He said: Five hundred years."
"1466","Abu al-Yaman told us: Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah told us, from Rashid ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about this verse: He is Able to send upon you torment from above you or from beneath your feet. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed it will be, and its interpretation has not yet come."
"1467","Ali ibn Ishaq told us: Abdullah informed us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: If what a fingernail carries of what is in Paradise appeared, the horizons of the heavens and the earth would be adorned for it, and if a man from the people of Paradise looked out and his bracelets appeared, its light would efface the light of the sun as the sun effaces the light of the stars."
"1468","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi told us: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, from his father, from his father, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I indeed saw on the right of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and on his left, on the Day of Uhud, two men wearing white clothes fighting on his behalf with the fiercest fighting; I never saw them before nor after."
"1469","Ishaq ibn Isa told us: Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to me, from his father, from Muadh al-Taymi, he said: I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Two prayers after which there is no prayer: dawn until the sun rises, and afternoon until the sun sets."
"1470","Yunus told us: Ibrahim told us, from his father, from a man from Banu Taym called Muadh, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"1471","Yaqub and Sad both said: My father told us, from his father, from his grandfather, Sad said: from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Sad ibn Abi Waqqas say: I indeed saw on the right of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and on his left, on the Day of Uhud, two men wearing white clothes fighting on his behalf with the fiercest fighting; I never saw them before nor after."
"1472","Yaqub told us: My father told us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd informed me, that Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed him, that his father Sad ibn Abi Waqqas said: Umar sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while with him were women from Quraysh speaking to him and asking much, their voices raised. When he sought permission, they stood hastening to the veil. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave him permission, meaning, so he entered, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was laughing. Then Umar said: May Allah make your tooth laugh, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I wondered at these who were with me; when they heard your voice they hastened to the veil. Umar said: It is you, O Messenger of Allah, whom they should have feared more. Then Umar said: O enemies of themselves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They said: Yes, you are harsher and more stern than the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Satan never met you walking a path but he walked a path other than your path. And Yaqub said: I cannot count what I heard him say: Salih told us, from Ibn Shihab."
"1473","Yaqub and Sad both said: My father told us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab: Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Jariyah narrated to me, that Yusuf ibn al-Hakam Abu al-Hajjaj informed him, that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will humiliate him."
"1474","Yahya ibn Said told us, from al-Jad ibn Aws, he said: Aishah bint Sad narrated to me, she said: Sad said: I complained of an illness of mine in Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me visiting me. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have left wealth, and I have only one daughter; shall I bequeath two thirds of my wealth and leave her a third. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath half and leave her half. He said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath a third and leave her two thirds. He said: A third, and a third is much, three times. He said: Then he placed his hand on his forehead and wiped my face and my chest and my belly, and said: O Allah, heal Sad and complete for him his emigration. I have ever since imagined I feel the coolness of his hand on my liver until this hour."
"1475","Yahya told us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, that Sad heard a man saying: At Your service, Possessor of the Ascensions. Then he said: He is indeed the Possessor of the Ascensions, but we were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and did not say that."
"1476","Waki told us: Said ibn Hassan al-Makhzumi told us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is not of us who does not chant the Quran. Waki said: Meaning, be sufficed by it."
"1477","Waki told us: Usamah ibn Zayd told us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah, from Sad ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best remembrance is the hidden, and the best provision is what suffices."
"1478","Ali ibn Ishaq told us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Usamah, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Uthman informed me, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah informed him. My father said: And Yahya, meaning al-Qattan, said: Ibn Abi Labibah also, except that he said: From Usamah, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah narrated to me."
"1479","Waki told us: Hisham told us, from his father, from Sad, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him visiting him while he was ill, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. He said: Then half. He said: No. He said: Then a third. He said: A third, and a third is much, or large."
"1480","Waki told us: Sufyan told us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Whatever you spend on your family of spending, you will be rewarded in it, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife."
"1481","Waki told us: Sufyan told us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severe in trial. He said: The prophets, then the righteous, then the next best, then the next best of people. A man is tried according to his religion; if there is firmness in his religion, his trial is increased, and if there is softness in his religion, it is lightened for him. And trial does not cease with the servant until he walks upon the back of the earth with no sin upon him."
"1482","Waki told us: Misar and Sufyan told us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, Sufyan said: from Amir ibn Sad, and Misar said: from some of the family of Sad, from Sad, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him visiting him while he was ill in Makkah. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. I said: Then half. He said: No. I said: Then a third. He said: A third, and a third is large, or much. That you leave your heir rich is better than that you leave him poor begging from people. And whatever you spend on your family of spending, you will be rewarded in it, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife. He said: And he had at that day only a daughter. Then Sad mentioned emigration, then he said: May Allah have mercy on Ibn Afra, and perhaps Allah will raise you so that a people benefit by you and others are harmed by you."
"1483","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi told us: Shubah told us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, he said: I heard Abu Abayah, from a freedman of Sad, that Sad heard a son of his supplicating, while he says: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and its bliss and its brocade and the like of this, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and its chains and its shackles. Then he said: You have asked Allah for much good and sought refuge in Allah from much evil, and I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be a people who transgress in supplication. And he recited this verse: Call upon your Lord humbly and secretly; He does not love the transgressors. And it suffices you to say: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and what brings near to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and what brings near to it of word or deed."
"1484","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Said both said: Abdullah ibn Jafar told us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, Abu Said said: He said: Ismail ibn Muhammad told us, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was, and Abu Said said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, give salaam to his right until the whiteness of his cheek was seen, and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek was seen."
"1485","Abd al-Rahman told us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him in Makkah while he was ill. Then he said: I have only one daughter, so shall I bequeath all my wealth. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath half of it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No. He said: Shall I bequeath a third of it. He said: A third, and a third is large."
"1486","Bahz told us: Hammam told us: Qatadah told us, from Abu Ghallab, from Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Malik, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him, then he mentioned the like of it. And Abd al-Samad said: Much, meaning: and a third."
"1487","Abd al-Rahman and Abd al-Razzaq, the meaning, both said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I wonder at the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for the believer: If good befalls him, he praises his Lord and thanks, and if a calamity befalls him, he praises his Lord and is patient. The believer is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to the mouth of his wife."
"1488","Abd al-Rahman told us, from Sufyan, from Sad, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to him visiting him while he was in Makkah, and he disliked dying in the land from which he had emigrated. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: May Allah have mercy on Sad ibn Afra; may Allah have mercy on Sad ibn Afra. And he had only one daughter. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shall I bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. He said: Then half. He said: No. He said: Then a third. He said: A third, and a third is much. That you leave your heirs rich is better than that you leave them dependent begging from people with what is in their hands. And whatever spending you spend, it is charity, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife. And perhaps Allah will raise you so that people benefit by you and others are harmed by you."
"1489","Abd al-Rahman told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar told us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Sad, he said: Make a grave with a side niche for me and set up over me as was done with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1490","Affan told us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, told us: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: I said to Sad ibn Malik: I want to ask you about a hadith, and I fear you to ask you about it. Then he said: Do not do it, O son of my brother; if you know that I have knowledge, ask me about it and do not fear me. He said: So I said: The statement of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Ali when he left him behind in Madinah in the raid of Tabuk. Then Sad said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left Ali behind in Madinah in the raid of Tabuk. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, do you leave me behind among those left behind, among women and children. Then he said: Are you not content to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Then Ali turned back hastening, as if I look at the dust of his feet rising. And Hammad said: Then Ali returned hastening."
"1491","Affan told us: Salim ibn Hayyan told us: Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to me: Yahya ibn Sad narrated to me, from his father, he said: Plague was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he said: A punishment with which those before you were afflicted; when it is in a land, do not enter it, and when it is in it and you are in it, do not leave it."
"1492","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I wonder at the believer: When good befalls him, he praises Allah and thanks, and when a calamity befalls him, he praises Allah and is patient. So the believer is rewarded in all his affair, even he is rewarded in the morsel he raises to the mouth of his wife."
"1493","Waki told us: Muhammad ibn Rashid told us, from Makhul, from Sad ibn Malik, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man who is the protector of the people, is his share and the share of another equal. He said: May your mother bereave you, O son of Umm Sad, are you provided and aided except by your weak."
"1494","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, he said: I heard Musab ibn Sad narrate, from Sad, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which people are most severe in trial. Then he said: The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to his religion; if his religion is thin, he is tried according to that, and if his religion is firm, he is tried according to that. He said: Trials do not cease with a man until he walks on the earth with no sin upon him."
"1495","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Sad ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, joined for me both his parents on the Day of Uhud."
"1496","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Abu Abdullah, freedman of Juhaynah, he said: I heard Musab ibn Sad narrate, from Sad, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Is one of you incapable of earning a thousand good deeds in a day. He said: And who can bear that. He said: He glorifies a hundred glorifications, and a thousand good deeds are written for him, and a thousand evil deeds are effaced from him."
"1497","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Asim al-Ahwal, he said: I heard Abu Uthman, he said: I heard Sad, and he is the first who shot an arrow in the path of Allah, and Abu Bakrah scaled the fortress of Taif among people, then came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Then they both said: We heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he says: Whoever claims to a father other than his father, while he knows that he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."
"1498","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Ismail, he said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Sad said: I indeed saw myself with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seventh of seven, and we had no food except leaves of the hublah tree, until one of us would drop as the sheep drops, with nothing mixed in it. Then Banu Asad came to discipline me about Islam; I would have lost then and my striving gone astray."
"1499","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Asim: Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever claims to other than his father, while he knows, Paradise is forbidden to him."
"1500","Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd informed us: Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas informed me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Sad, stand and call in Mina: They are days of eating and drinking, and there is no fasting in them."
"1501","Al-Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us from Za'idah from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami who said: Sa'd said: Concerning me the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established the Sunnah of the third. He came to visit me. He said: He said to me: Have you made a bequest. He said: I said: Yes, I have made all my wealth for the poor and needy and the traveler. He said: Do not do it. I said: My heirs are rich. I said: Two thirds. He said: No. I said: Then half. He said: No. I said: The third. He said: The third, and the third is much."
"1502","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Sa'd ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no hamah and no contagion and no tiyarah; if it be, then in the woman and the mount and the house."
"1503","He said: I read before Abd al-Rahman from Malik. My father said, and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas informed us from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn Abd al-Muttalib that he narrated to him that he heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and al-Dahhak ibn Qays in the year Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan performed Hajj, while they were mentioning tamattu' with Umrah to Hajj. Al-Dahhak said: None does that except one who is ignorant of the command of Allah. Sa'd said: Evil is what you have said, O son of my brother. Al-Dahhak said: Umar ibn al-Khattab forbade that. Sa'd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it, and we did it with him."
"1504","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi who said: Sa'd said, and once he said: I heard Sa'd say: My ears heard it and my heart retained it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that whoever claims a father other than his father while he knows that he is other than his father, then Paradise is forbidden to him. He said: I met Abu Bakrah and narrated it to him. He said: And my ears heard it and my heart retained it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1505","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim who said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrating from Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa."
"1506","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj, Shu'bah narrated to me from Qatadah from Yunus ibn Jubayr from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus that corrupts it is better for him than to be filled with poetry. Hajjaj said: I heard Yunus ibn Jubayr."
"1507","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Qatadah from Umar ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from Sa'd from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus until it corrupts him is better than to be filled with poetry."
"1508","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Qatadah from Ikrimah from Ibn Sa'd from Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said concerning the plague: If it occurs in a land, do not enter it, and if you are in it, do not flee from it. Shu'bah said: And Hisham Abu Bakr narrated to me that he is Ikrimah ibn Khalid."
"1509","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd who said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: I said to Sa'd ibn Malik: You are a man in whom there is sharpness, and I want to ask you. He said: What is it. He said: I said: The hadith of Ali. He said: He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa. He said: I am pleased. Then he said: Yes, yes."
"1510","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Awn from Jabir ibn Samurah, and Bahz and Affan both said: Shu'bah narrated to us, Abu Awn informed me, Bahz said: He said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: Umar said to Sa'd: The people have complained about you in everything, even in prayer. He said: As for me, I prolong the first two and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short in following the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar said: That is my opinion of you, or my supposition of you."
"1511","Hajjaj narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Sharik from Abd Allah ibn al-Ruqaym al-Kinani who said: We went out to Madinah at the time of al-Jamal, and Sa'd ibn Malik met us there. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the doors opening into the mosque to be blocked, and the door of Ali to be left."
"1512","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth informed us, and Abu al-Nadr, Layth narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Mulaykah al-Qurashi then al-Taymi narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Abi Nahik from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: He is not from us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously."
"1513","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth informed us, Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to come to his family by night after the Isha prayer."
"1514","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth informed us, Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab, Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed me that he heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas say: Uthman ibn Maz'un wanted to practice celibacy, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him; had he permitted that to him, we would have castrated ourselves."
"1515","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Yazid, freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, narrated to me from Abu Ayyash from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about fresh dates for dry dates. He said: Does not the fresh date decrease when it dries. They said: Yes. So he disliked it."
"1516","Ya'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us from his father who said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we passed the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah. He entered and prayed two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him, and he conversed with his Lord, mighty and majestic, for a long time. He said: I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, for three things. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by famine, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make their violence among them, and He withheld it from me."
"1517","Ya'la and Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya said: A man whose name I used to name but I forgot his name narrated to me from Umar ibn Sa'd who said: I had a need to Abu Sa'd. He said, and Abu Hayyan narrated to us from Mujammi' who said: Umar ibn Sa'd had a need to his father, so he presented before his need some speech from what people relate, seeking to connect, which he had not heard. When he finished, he said: O my son, have you finished your speech. He said: Yes. He said: You were never farther from your need, nor was I more indifferent to you, than since I heard this speech of yours. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be people who eat with their tongues as the cow eats from the earth."
"1518","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd to Umar, and they said: He does not pray well. He said: Umar asked him. He said: I pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I remain calm in the first two and shorten the last two. He said: That is my opinion of you, O Abu Ishaq."
"1519","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Abu Ishaq from Umar ibn Sa'd, Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to us who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting the believer is disbelief, and abusing him is transgression, and it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"1520","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the greatest of Muslims in crime against Muslims is a man who asked about something and probed into it until prohibition concerning that thing was revealed because of his asking."
"1521","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Umar ibn Sa'd or another that Sa'd ibn Malik said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever degrades Quraysh, Allah, mighty and majestic, degrades him."
"1522","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave men and did not give a man among them anything. Sa'd said: O Prophet of Allah, you gave so-and-so and so-and-so, and you did not give so-and-so anything, while he is a believer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim, until Sa'd repeated it three times, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept saying: Or a Muslim. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give men and leave one who is more beloved to me than them, and I do not give him anything, fearing that they will be thrown into the Fire on their faces."
"1523","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of the gecko and called it a little transgressor."
"1524","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj, and I fell ill with an illness in which I came near death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and none inherits me except a daughter of mine; shall I bequeath two thirds of my wealth. He said: No. I said: Half my wealth. He said: No. I said: Then a third of my wealth. He said: The third, and the third is much. You, O Sa'd, to leave your heirs rich is better for you than to leave them dependent begging from people. You, O Sa'd, will not spend any spending seeking thereby the Face of Allah, exalted, except you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you place in the mouth of your wife. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind after my companions. He said: You will not be left behind and do a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah except you will increase thereby in degree and elevation, and perhaps you will be left behind until Allah benefits peoples through you and harms others through you. O Allah, carry out for my Companions their hijrah, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched Sa'd ibn Khawlah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt pity for him, and he had died in Makkah."
"1525","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri who said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab informed me from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected celibacy for Uthman; had he permitted it, we would have castrated ourselves."
"1526","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from his father from his grandfather that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was no prophet except he described the Dajjal to his ummah, and I shall describe him with a description that none before me described: he is one-eyed, and Allah, mighty and majestic, is not one-eyed."
"1527","Abd al-Samad and Affan narrated to us, both said: Sulaym ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Affan said: He narrated to me from Yahya ibn Sa'd from Sa'd that the plague was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: It is a punishment with which those before you were afflicted; if it is in a land, do not enter it, and if you are in a land and it is in it, do not leave it."
"1528","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar who said: Amir ibn Sa'd narrated to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, while he was governor over Madinah, that Sa'd said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats seven Ajwah dates between the two lava tracts of Madinah in the morning, nothing will harm him that day until evening. Fulayh said: And I think he said: And if he eats them in the evening, nothing will harm him until morning. He said: Umar said: O Amir, look at what you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Amir said: By Allah, I did not lie against Sa'd, and Sa'd did not lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1529","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd al-Aslami narrated to us from al-Muttalib from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father that he said: His son Amir came to him and said: O my son, in the fitnah do you order me to be a head. No, by Allah, until I am given a sword, if I strike a believer with it, it turns away from him, and if I strike a disbeliever with it, it kills him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, mighty and majestic, loves the rich, hidden, pious."
"1530","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from his father from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I saw on the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and on his left on the day of Uhud two men wearing white clothes whom I had not seen before nor after."
"1531","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Ayzar from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father Sa'd from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I wonder at the Muslim: when good befalls him he praises Allah and thanks, and when calamity befalls him he expects reward and endures. The Muslim is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."
"1532","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Qatadah and Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, both said: Ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, a son of Sa'd ibn Malik narrated to me a hadith from his father who said: I entered upon Sa'd and said: A hadith I was told from you when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ali over Madinah. He said: He became angry and said: Who narrated it to you. I disliked to tell him that his son had narrated it to me, lest he become angry with him. Then he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the expedition of Tabuk, he left Ali over Madinah. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, I would not love that you go out in any direction except that I am with you. He said: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"1533","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Malik, meaning Ibn Anas, narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us from Amir ibn Sa'd who said: I heard my father say: I did not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say of any living one walking that he is in Paradise except for Abd Allah ibn Salam."
"1534","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abdullah said, and I heard it myself from Harun, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah narrated to me from his father from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I heard Sa'd and people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There were two brothers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them was better than the other. The one who was the better of them died, then the other lived after him forty nights, then died. The excellence of the first over the other was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Did he not pray. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and there was no harm in him. He said: What makes you know what his prayer reached. Then he said at that: The parable of the prayers is as the parable of a flowing river at the door of a man, deep, sweet, he plunges into it every day five times; what do you think that leaves of his dirt."
"1535","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Yunus ibn Jubayr from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus and blood is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"1536","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me who said: I came to Madinah, and we heard that the plague had occurred in Kufah. He said: I said: Who narrates this hadith. It was said: Amir ibn Sa'd. He said: He was absent, so I met Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, and he narrated to me that he heard Usamah ibn Zayd narrating to Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the plague occurs in a land, do not enter it, and if it occurs while you are in it, do not leave it. He said: I said: Did you hear Usamah. He said: Yes."
"1537","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us from Zakariyya from Abu Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting the Muslim is disbelief, and abusing him is transgression."
"1538","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr informed us from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Sa'd ibn Malik who said: He said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has healed me of the polytheists, so grant me this sword. He said: This sword is neither yours nor mine, put it down. He said: I put it down, then I returned and said: Perhaps this sword today will be given to one who did not exert as I exerted. He said: Then a man called me from behind. He said: I said: Something has been revealed concerning me. He said: You asked me for the sword, and it was not mine, and it has been granted to me, so it is yours. He said: And this verse was revealed: They ask you about the spoils. Say: The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger."
"1539","Abdullah narrated to us who said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting: Abd al-Muta'al ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to me, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to me, Abu Abd al-Rahman said, and Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Mujalid narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah, Juhaynah came to him and said: You have settled among us, so make a covenant for us until we come to you and you grant us security. So he made a covenant for them, and they embraced Islam. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in Rajab, not being a hundred, and ordered us to raid a clan of Banu Kinanah next to Juhaynah. We raided them, and they were many, so we sought refuge with Juhaynah, and they protected us and said: Why do you fight in the sacred month. We said: We fight only one who expelled us from the sacred city in the sacred month. Some of us said to others: What do you think. Some said: We come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him. People said: No, rather we stay here. I said, with people with me: No, rather we come to the caravan of Quraysh and intercept it. We went to the caravan, and spoils then was whoever took something it is his. We went to the caravan, and our companions went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the report. He stood angry, red-faced, and said: You went from me all together and came divided. Those before you were destroyed only by division. I shall surely send over you a man, not the best of you, the most patient of you over hunger and thirst. So he sent over us Abd Allah ibn Jahsh al-Asadi, and he was the first commander appointed in Islam."
"1540","Husayn narrated to us from Za'idah from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, and Abd al-Samad, Za'idah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us from Jabir ibn Samurah and from Nafi' ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will fight the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will open it for you. Then you will fight Persia, and Allah will open it for you. Then you will fight Rome, and Allah will open it for you. Then you will fight the Dajjal, and Allah will open him for you. He said: Jabir said: The Dajjal will not emerge until Rome is opened."
"1541","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us from Jabir ibn Samurah from Nafi' ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will raid the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will open it for you. You will raid Persia, and Allah will open it for you. You will raid Rome, and Allah will open it for you. You will raid the Dajjal, and Allah will open him for you."
"1542","Ya'qub narrated to us who said: I heard my father narrating from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that the owners of farms in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lease their farms with what is on the water channels of crops and what is watered by water around the plants. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and disputed concerning some of that. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to lease with that, and said: Lease with gold and silver."
"1543","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, and Ya'qub, my father narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq narrated to me, Ya'qub said: Ibn Abi Atiq, from Amir ibn Sa'd, he narrated to him from his father Sa'd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If one of you spits in the mosque, let him conceal his spittle lest it touch the skin of a believer or his garment and harm him."
"1544","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Malik from Abd Allah ibn Yazid from Zayd ibn Ayyash who said: Sa'd was asked about white wheat for sult. He disliked it and said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about fresh dates for dry dates. He said: Does it decrease when it dries. They said: Yes. He said: Then no."
"1545","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The greatest of Muslims in crime against Muslims is one who asked about a matter not forbidden, then it was forbidden for people because of his asking."
"1546","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father who said: I fell ill in Makkah in the year of the Conquest with a severe illness in which I came near death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and none inherits me except my daughter; shall I give charity of two thirds of my wealth, and Sufyan once said: Shall I give charity of my wealth. He said: No. He said: Shall I give charity of two thirds of my wealth. He said: No. I said: Then half. He said: No. He said: I said: The third. He said: The third, and the third is great. For you to leave your heirs rich is better than to leave them dependent begging from people. You will not spend any spending except you will be rewarded in it, even the morsel you raise to the mouth of your wife. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind from my hijrah. He said: You will not be left behind after me and do a deed seeking thereby the Face of Allah except you will increase thereby in elevation and degree, and perhaps you will be left behind until peoples benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O Allah, carry out for my Companions their hijrah, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched Sa'd ibn Khawlah, he felt pity for him that he died in Makkah."
"1547","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Sa'd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me in the position of Harun to Musa. It was said to Sufyan: Except that there is no prophet after me. He said: He said: Yes."
"1548","Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Malik, he heard it from Jabir ibn Samurah: The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd to Umar, and they said: He does not pray well. He said: By Allah concerning the Bedouins, I do not fall short with them from the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr; I remain calm in the first two and shorten the last two. I heard Umar say: Such is my opinion of you, O Abu Ishaq."
"1549","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr, I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nahik from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously."
"1550","Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from al-Zuhri from Malik ibn Aws, I heard Umar say to Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Talhah and al-Zubayr and Sa'd: I adjure you by Allah by whom the heaven and the earth stand, and once he said: by whose permission it stands, do you know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We are not inherited; what we leave is charity. They said: O Allah, yes."
"1551","Sufyan narrated to us from al-Ala, meaning Ibn Abi al-Abbas, from Abu al-Tufayl from Bakr ibn Qirwash from Sa'd. It was said to Sufyan: From the Prophet. He said: Yes. He said: The devil of al-Radhah, he guards it, meaning a man from Bajilah."
"1552","Sufyan narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Umayyah from Abd Allah ibn Yazid from Abu Ayyash who said: Sa'd was asked about selling sult for barley or something like this. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about dates for fresh dates. He said: Does the fresh decrease when it dries. They said: Yes. He said: Then no."
"1553","Isma'il narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi who said: I heard Sa'd say: My ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That whoever claims to other than his father while he knows that he is other than his father, then Paradise is forbidden to him. He said: I met Abu Bakrah and narrated it to him. He said: And my ears heard and my heart retained from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1554","Isma'il narrated to us, Hisham al-Dustuwa'i informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab who said: I asked Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas about tiyarah, and he rebuked me and said: Who narrated to you. I disliked to tell him who had narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion and no tiyarah and no hamah; if tiyarah be in anything, then in the horse and the woman and the house; and if you hear of the plague in a land, do not descend upon it, and if it is in a land while you are in it, do not flee from it."
"1555","Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ibrahim, narrated to us, Hisham al-Dustuwa'i informed us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd who said: Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severe in trial. He said: The prophets, then the best, then the best, until the servant is tried according to his religion; that is, if he is firm in religion, he is tried according to that, and he said once: most severe in trial, and if there is softness in his religion, he is tried according to that, and he said once: according to his religion. He said: Trials do not leave the servant until he walks on the earth, meaning, with no sin upon him. My father said: And he said once: from Sa'd who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah."
"1557","Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd to Umar, and they said: He does not pray well. Umar mentioned that to him. He said: As for the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to pray with them; I remain calm in the first two and shorten the last two. He said: That is my opinion of you, O Abu Ishaq."
"1558","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Umar ibn Nubayh, Abu Abd Allah al-Qarraz narrated to me who said: I heard Sa'd ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever intends the people of Madinah with destruction or evil, Allah melts him as salt melts in water."
"1559","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Usamah ibn Zayd, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah narrated to me from Sa'd ibn Malik from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best remembrance is the hidden, and the best provision is what suffices."
"1560","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us from Ibn al-Mubarak from Usamah who said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman informed me that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah informed him, and he mentioned it."
"1561","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Musa al-Juhani, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to me from his father that a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me words I say. He said: Say: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, Allah is Most Great, much, and praise be to Allah abundantly, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, the Mighty, the Wise, five. He said: These are for my Lord, so what is for me. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me and have mercy on me and provide for me and guide me and grant me health."
"1562","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, narrated to us who said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: I heard Sa'd say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me his two parents on the day of Uhud."
"1563","Yahya narrated to us from Musa, meaning al-Juhani, Mus'ab ibn Sa'd narrated to me, my father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to earn every day a thousand good deeds. A man from his companions said: How does one of us earn a thousand good deeds. He said: He glorifies a hundred glorifications; a thousand good deeds are written for him, or a thousand sins are removed from him. My father said, and Ibn Numayr also said: Or removed, and Ya'la also: Or removed."
"1564","Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to me from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd from Amir ibn Sa'd from his father Sa'd ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to greet to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheeks was seen."
"1565","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from al-Hukaym ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father Sa'd that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he hears the mu'adhdhin: And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, we are pleased with Allah as Lord and with Muhammad as Messenger and with Islam as religion, his sin is forgiven. Qutaybah narrated it to us from Layth from al-Hukaym ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays."
"1566","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Qays narrated to us who said: I heard Sa'd ibn Malik say: I am the first of the Arabs who shot an arrow in the path of Allah, and we came raiding with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we had no food to eat except the leaves of the hublah and this samar, until one of us would excrete as the sheep excretes, having no mixture. Then Banu Asad came to rebuke me concerning religion. I would have failed then and my deed would have been lost."
"1567","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Shu'bah, Simak ibn Harb narrated to me from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd who said: Four verses were revealed concerning my father. He said: My father said: I took a sword. I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me. He said: Put it down. I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me; shall I be made as one who has no avail. He said: Put it down where you took it. Then it was revealed: They ask you about the spoils, and it is in the recitation of Ibn Mas'ud likewise: Say: The spoils. My mother said: Does not Allah command you to maintain kinship and honor parents. By Allah, I will not eat food nor drink drink until you disbelieve in Muhammad. She would not eat until they pried open her mouth with a stick and poured drink into it. Shu'bah said: And I think he said: And food. Then it was revealed: And We enjoined man concerning his parents, his mother bore him in weakness upon weakness, and he recited until he reached: With what you used to do. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was ill. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth. He forbade me. I said: Half. He said: No. I said: The third. He kept silent. So the people took it. A man from the Ansar made food, and they ate and drank and became intoxicated from wine, and that was before it was forbidden. We gathered with him and boasted. The Ansar said: The Ansar are best. The Muhajirun said: The Muhajirun are best. A man reached for him with a jawbone of a camel and split his nose. The nose of Sa'd was split. Then it was revealed: O you who believe, wine and gambling, to His saying: Will you then desist."
"1568","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us, Ghunaym narrated to me who said: I asked Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas about mut'ah. He said: We did it, and this is a disbeliever in the Throne, meaning Mu'awiyah."
"1569","Yahya narrated to us from Shu'bah from Qatadah from Yunus ibn Jubayr from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the belly of a man to be filled with pus is better than to be filled with poetry."
"1570","Yahya narrated to us from Isma'il from al-Zubayr ibn Adi from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd who said: I prayed with Sa'd, and I put my hands like this, and Yahya described tatbiq. He struck my hands and said: We used to do this, then we were ordered to raise to the knees."
"1571","Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hashim narrated to us from A'ishah bint Sa'd from Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes the morning with seven Ajwah dates, neither poison nor magic will harm him that day."
"1572","Makki narrated to us, Hashim narrated to us from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from Sa'd, and he mentioned the hadith the same as it. Abu Badr narrated it to us from Hashim from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas."
"1573","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from Uthman, meaning Ibn Hakim, Amir ibn Sa'd informed me from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I declare sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah, that its thorn trees be cut or its game killed. He said: Madinah is better for them had they known. None leaves it disliking it except Allah replaces in it one who is better than him. None remains steadfast over its hardship and effort except I will be for him a witness or an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"1574","Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us from Uthman who said: Amir ibn Sa'd informed me from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came one day from al-Aliyah until when he passed the mosque of Banu Mu'awiyah, he entered and bowed in it two rak'ahs, and we prayed with him, and he supplicated his Lord for a long time. Then he turned to us and said: I asked my Lord for three; He gave me two and withheld from me one. I asked my Lord not to destroy my ummah by famine, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drowning, and He granted it to me. I asked Him not to make their violence among them, and He withheld it from me."
"1575","Waki' narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth al-Abdi from Umar ibn Sa'd from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I wonder at the believer: if good befalls him he praises Allah and thanks, and if calamity befalls him he expects reward and endures. The believer is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."
"1576","Waki' narrated to us, Ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from al-Zubayr ibn Adi from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd who said: When I bowed I placed my hands between my knees. He said: My father Sa'd ibn Malik saw me and forbade me and said: We used to do it, then we were forbidden from it."
"1577","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd from Sa'd ibn Malik and Khuzaymah ibn Thabit and Usamah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This plague is a punishment or a remainder of a torment with which peoples before you were punished. If it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it fleeing from it, and if you hear of it in a land, do not enter upon it."
"1578","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Dawud ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely describe the Dajjal with a description that none before me described: he is one-eyed, and Allah, mighty and majestic, is not one-eyed."
"1579","Yazid narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us from al-Zuhri from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a group came to him and asked him, and he gave them except a man among them. Sa'd said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, you gave them and left so-and-so; by Allah, I see him a believer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. Sa'd repeated that to him three times, believer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to him: Or a Muslim. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the third time: By Allah, I give a man a gift, another more beloved to me than him, fearing that Allah will throw him on his face into the Fire."
"1580","He said: Abu Nu'aym said: I met Sufyan in Makkah, and the first who asked me about him, he said: How is Shuja', meaning Abu Badr."
"1581","Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, and Hashim ibn al-Qasim, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Salih ibn Kaysan, Hashim said in his hadith: He said: Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me, and Yazid said: from Salih from al-Zuhri from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him were women from Quraysh asking him and demanding much, raising their voices. When they heard the voice of Umar, they restrained themselves and fell silent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed. Umar said: O enemies of yourselves, do you fear me and not fear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: You are harsher than the Messenger of Allah and sterner. The Messenger of Allah said: O Umar, Satan never met you walking a path except he took a path other than yours."
"1582","Yazid narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us from Muhammad ibn Ikrimah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Labibah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Sa'd ibn Malik who said: We used to lease land in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with what is on the water channels of crops and with what is watered by water of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that, and permitted us, or allowed, to lease it with gold and silver."
"1583","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ali ibn Abi Talib behind in the expedition of Tabuk. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do you leave me behind among the women and children. He said: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"1584","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq informed me who said: I heard Qays ibn Abayah narrating from a freedman of Sa'd. My father said, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq who said: I heard Qays ibn Abayah al-Qaysi narrating from a freedman of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from a son of Sa'd that he used to pray and say in his supplication: O Allah, I ask You Paradise, and I ask You of its bliss and splendor and of such and of such and of such and of such, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and its chains and fetters and from such and from such. He said: Sa'd kept silent from him. When he prayed, Sa'd said to him: You sought refuge from a great evil and asked for a great bliss, or he said: long, Shu'bah doubted. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be people who transgress in supplication. And he recited: Call upon your Lord humbly and secretly; He does not love the transgressors. Shu'bah said: I do not know whether His saying: Call upon your Lord humbly and secretly is from the saying of Sa'd or the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sa'd said to him: Say: O Allah, I ask You Paradise and what brings near to it of word or deed, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and what brings near to it of word or deed."
"1585","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Mus'ab from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that he used to command these five and report them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You that I be returned to the worst of age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the world, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave."
"1586","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan ibn al-Ala ibn Jariyah from Yusuf ibn al-Hakam Abu al-Hajjaj from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah, mighty and majestic, humiliates him."
"1587","Abu Kamil narrated to us another time, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan ibn al-Ala ibn Jariyah from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father Sa'd who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever intends the humiliation of Quraysh, Allah humiliates him."
"1588","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab who said: I heard Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rejected celibacy for Uthman ibn Maz'un; had he permitted him in it, we would have castrated ourselves."
"1589","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Malik from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three."
"1590","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father who said: I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. My companions said: You have said evil. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The covenant was near, and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: There is no god but Allah alone, three times, then spit to your left three times, and seek refuge, and do not return."
"1591","Abu Abd al-Rahman Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il and Affan, the meaning, both said: Hammad narrated to us, Asim narrated to us from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl of tharid, and he ate, and some leftover remained of it. He said: There will enter from this pass a man from the people of Paradise eating this leftover. Sa'd said: I had left my brother Umayr ibn Abi Waqqas preparing to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I hoped that it is he. Then Abd Allah ibn Salam came and ate it."
"1592","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: I passed by Uwaymir ibn Malik."
"1593","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Usamah, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Abu Abd Allah al-Qarraz narrated to us that he heard Sa'd ibn Malik and Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their city, and bless them in their sa', and bless them in their mudd. O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and friend, and I am Your servant and Messenger, and Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and I ask You for the people of Madinah as Ibrahim asked You for the people of Makkah, and like it with it. Madinah is netted with angels; over every pass of it are two angels guarding it. Neither plague nor the Dajjal enters it. Whoever intends it with evil, Allah melts him as salt melts in water."
"1594","Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us striking one hand on the other, saying: The month is like this and like this. Then he decreased a finger in the third."
"1595","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us from Isma'il from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The month is like this and like this, ten and ten and nine at once."
"1596","al-Talaqani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Isma'il from Muhammad ibn Sa'd from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The month is like this and like this and like this, meaning twenty-nine."
"1597","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning al-Darawardi, narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people emerge who eat with their tongues as cows eat with their tongues."
"1598","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Hasan narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir from Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Hafs, and he mentioned a story. Sa'd said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Good is the death for a man to die defending his right."
"1599","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us from his uncle Jarir, meaning Ibn Zayd, from Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas from his father Sa'd who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. I said: Then two thirds. He said: No. I said: Then half. He said: No. I said: Then the third. He said: The third, and the third is great. For one of you to leave his family in good is better for him than to leave them dependent on the hands of people."
"1600","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Habib ibn Abi Thabit, narrated to us from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah from his father from Sa'd who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in the expedition of Tabuk, he left Ali behind. He said to him: Do you leave me behind. He said to him: Are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"1601","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar told us: Ismail ibn Muhammad told us, from Amir ibn Sad, that Sad said in his illness: When I die, make a lahd for me and do just as was done for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1602","Mansur ibn Salamah al-Khuzai told us: Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, from Ismail ibn Muhammad, from Amir ibn Sad, from Sad, he said: Make a lahd for me and set up unbaked bricks over me as was done for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"1603","Surayj ibn al-Numan told us: Abu Shihab told us, from al-Hajjaj, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Sad ibn Malik, he said: We performed tawaf with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; some of us did tawaf seven times and some eight times and some more than that, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No harm."
"1604","Harun ibn Maruf told us: Abdullah ibn Wahb informed us: Abu Sakhr informed me; Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: And I myself heard it from Harun: that Abu Hazim narrated to him, from a son of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Faith began strange and will return as it began, so glad tidings that day for the strangers when people become corrupt. By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, faith will retreat between these two mosques as the snake retreats into its hole."
"1605","Sulayman ibn Dawud told us: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi al-Zinad, informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"1606","Affan told us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad told us: Uthman ibn Hakim informed us: Amir ibn Sad narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I declare sacred what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah as Ibrahim declared his sanctuary sacred. Its thorn trees are not to be cut, its game is not to be killed, and no one leaves it out of dislike for it except that Allah replaces him with someone better than him. And Madinah is better for them if they only knew. And no one intends harm against its people except that Allah melts him as lead melts in fire, or as salt melts in water."
"1607","Affan told us: Hammad ibn Zayd told us: Asim ibn Bahdalah told us: Musab ibn Sad narrated to me, from his father, he said: I said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Which people are most severely tried. He said: The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to his religion; if his religion is firm his trial is severe, and if there is softness in his religion he is tried according to his religion. Trial keeps befalling the servant until it leaves him walking on the earth with no sin upon him."
"1608","Qutaybah ibn Said told us: Hatim ibn Ismail told us, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying to him, when he left him behind in one of his expeditions, and Ali said: Are you leaving me behind with the women and children. He said: O Ali, are you not pleased to be to me in the position of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophethood after me. And I heard him saying on the day of Khaybar: I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. So we stretched our necks toward it, then he said: Call Ali for me. So he was brought with sore eyes, and he spat in his eyes and handed the banner to him, and Allah granted victory through him. And when this verse was revealed: Let us call our sons and your sons, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Ali and Fatimah and Hasan and Husayn and said: O Allah, these are my family."
"1609","Qutaybah ibn Said told us: Layth ibn Sad told us, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Busr ibn Said, that Sad ibn Abi Waqqas said at the time of the fitnah of Uthman ibn Affan: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be a fitnah; the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one running. He said: What do you think, if he enters upon me in my house and stretches his hand toward me to kill me. He said: Be like the son of Adam."
"1610","Ali ibn Abdullah told us: Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi of the people of Madinah narrated to me: Abu Suhayl Nafi ibn Malik narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to al-Abbas: This is al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most joining of kin."
"1611","Abdullah ibn Numayr and Yala said: Musa, meaning al-Juhani, told us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, teach me words I may say. He said: Say: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner; Allah is Most Great, greatly; praise be to Allah abundantly; glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; there is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Mighty, the Wise. He said: These are for my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, so what is for me. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me. Ibn Numayr said: Musa said: As for grant me health, I am imagining it and I do not know."
"1612","Abdullah ibn Numayr told us: Musa told us, from Musab ibn Sad: My father narrated to me, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day. A questioner among his companions asked him: O Prophet of Allah, how does one of us earn a thousand good deeds. He said: He glorifies Allah a hundred glorifications, and a thousand good deeds are written for him or a thousand sins are wiped away from him."
"1613","Yala ibn Ubayd told us: Musa told us, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Is any one of you unable to earn a thousand good deeds every day. A questioner among his companions asked him: How does one of us earn, O Messenger of Allah, a thousand good deeds every day. He said: He glorifies Allah a hundred glorifications, and a thousand good deeds are written for him or a thousand sins are wiped away from him."
"1614","Muhammad ibn Jafar told us: Shubah told us, from Simak, from Musab ibn Sad, from his father, he said: Four verses were revealed concerning me on the day of Badr. I took a sword, then I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me as extra spoils. He said: Put it down. Then he stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me as extra spoils; make me like one who has no means. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Put it down where you took it from. Then this verse was revealed: They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger. He said: And a man of the Ansar made food and invited us, and we drank wine until we became intoxicated. He said: And the Ansar and Quraysh boasted against each other; the Ansar said: We are better than you, and Quraysh said: We are better than you. So a man of the Ansar took a camel jawbone and struck the nose of Sad with it and split it. He said: And the nose of Sad was split. He said: Then this verse was revealed: O you who believe, wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are filth from the work of Satan, so avoid them that you may prosper. He said: And the mother of Sad said: Has not Allah commanded them to be dutiful; by Allah, I will not taste food nor drink drink until I die or you disbelieve in Muhammad. He said: And when they wanted to feed her they pried her mouth open with a stick then poured food in. He said: Then this verse was revealed: And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon Sad while he was ill visiting him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I bequeath all my wealth. He said: No. He said: Then two thirds. He said: No. He said: Then a third. He said: Then he fell silent."
"1615","Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi told us: Aban told us: Yahya told us, from al-Hadrami ibn Lahiq, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Sad ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the plague is in a land, do not go down upon it, and when it is in a land and you are in it, do not flee from it."
"1616","Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Sad ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said on the day of Uhud: Shoot; may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"1617","Yazid ibn Harun told us: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Yahya ibn Ubayd al-Bahrani, from Muhammad ibn Sad, he said: And he used to perform ablution at al-Zawiyah, then he came out to us one day from relieving himself and performed ablution and wiped over his khuffs, and we were amazed and said: What is this. He said: My father narrated to me that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, doing just as I did."
"1618","Yazid ibn Harun told us: Ismail informed us, from Qays, he said: I heard Sad ibn Malik saying: By Allah, I am the first of the Arabs to shoot an arrow in the cause of Allah. We used to raid with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we had no food to eat except the leaves of the hublah and this samur, until one of us would pass droppings as the sheep passes, having no mixture in it. Then Banu Asad began to reproach me over religion; if so I would indeed have failed and my deed would have been lost."
"1619","Yazid informed us: Abu Mashar informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, giving salams to his right and to his left."
"1620","Rawh told us: Ibn Awn told us, from Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Aswad, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, he said: On the day of al-Khandaq, when a man was shielding himself, he kept saying with the shield like this, putting it above his nose, then saying like this, lowering it afterward. He said: So I reached for my quiver and took out a feathered arrow from it and placed it in the middle of the bow, and when he said like this lowering the shield, I shot, and I have not forgotten the striking of the arrowhead on such and such part of the shield. He said: And he fell and said with his leg, and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laughed, I think he said, until his molars appeared. He said: I said: Why. He said: Because of what the man did."
"1621","Rawh told us: Shubah told us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Musab ibn Sad narrating from his father Sad ibn Abi Waqqas that he used to enjoin this supplication and narrate it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from being returned to the most decrepit age, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of this world, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave."
"1622","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Said said: Israil told us, from Abu Ishaq; Abu Said said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Musab ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, that he swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza, so his companions said to him: You have uttered an obscenity. So he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: The covenant was recent and I swore by al-Lat and al-Uzza. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Say: There is no god but Allah alone, three times, and spit to your left three times, and seek refuge in Allah from Satan, and do not return to it."
"1623","Uthman ibn Umar told us: Usamah told us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Labibah, that Sad ibn Malik said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best remembrance is the hidden, and the best provision is what suffices."
"1624","Abu Dawud Sulayman told us: Ibrahim ibn Sad told us, from Salih ibn Kaysan: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from his father, he said: Umar sought permission from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while with him were slave girls whose voices had risen above his voice, so he gave him permission and they hastened away. Then Umar entered while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was laughing, so Umar said: May Allah keep your teeth laughing, O Messenger of Allah; may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: I was amazed at slave girls who were with me; when they heard your voice they hastened away. Then he turned to them and said: O enemies of your own selves, by Allah, you were more deserving to be in awe of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, than of me. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave them from you, O Umar; by Allah, Satan never meets you on a path but that he takes a path other than your path. This is the end of the hadith of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him."
